// osprey: flavor=ml
// Must-reject. Pins [FLAVOR-ML-FN]/[FLAVOR-ML-CURRY] (docs/specs/0024): a
// parenthesised signature domain describes the FLAT binding form, so pairing
// it with a curried binding is a form mismatch the lowering must reject.
//
// This program used to COMPILE AND RUN: a tuple type has no canonical TypeExpr
// form, so the lowering dropped the whole written domain and checked the
// binding as if unannotated — the signature below disagrees with the binding
// in arity AND types, the call site passes a string where the signature says
// int, and it printed `p=wrong type entirely`. A written signature the checker
// never consults is the exact silent miscompile stabilization forbids. The
// arity and too-short-spine twins of this case are pinned in
// crates/osprey-syntax/tests/ml_coverage.rs.
f : (int, string, bool) -> string
f p = "p=${p}"

print (f "wrong type entirely")
